# Article writing

Stay close to the source article. Blog integration is light-touch only: Jekyll front matter, working links, and code/examples aligned to a real repo when one exists. Do not rewrite voice, add slogans, or invent framing the source did not use.

## Do not add brand asides

- Do not insert "thinking inside the box", "the box", or other publication taglines unless the source already uses them or the user explicitly asks.
- Do not add series recaps, editorial philosophy paragraphs, or mascot copy to the body.

## Demo repos

- Treat linked repositories as **example implementations**, not "reference architectures", unless the user says otherwise.
- Do not lead the article with the repo. Introduce it when the piece turns to concrete implementation — typically the later pillars or the closing section.

## What to change

- Front matter (`layout`, `date`, `categories`, `topics`, `projects`, `image`, `description`, `external_repo`).
- Code samples and named tools/metrics so they match the demo.
- Broken markdown (missing fences, escaped characters).

Leave the rest of the source intact.
